r@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="395730" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/30/395730/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9ade9de068589dce6995cda6b106217aa85aa793" commit="b105e8037c90e0718d592aefe2885058aa0bc55d" commit_message="pd: Initialize pd comms and dual role state from PD task  Don't call into tcpm_*() functions from HOOKs since these functions may manipulate common sets of TCPC registers.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57691 BRANCH=gru TEST=On kevin, boot to S0, verify 5V is sourced to legacy peripheral. Drop to G3, verify role is back to sink and charging is functional. Back to S0, verify 5V is sourced.  Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I9ade9de068589dce6995cda6b106217aa85aa793 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394809 (cherry picked from commit 18e9e3870722d57efd232bd7f0a0300003b46ad6) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/396137 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="396137" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/37/396137/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="I4d1576dd95388a95d85340ada95ba34a73bc4cf2" commit="fcb9cc2193b75e6d957f654ce6386337c9d72aad" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iwl7000: mvm: show TX power configuration in debugfs  Show the TX power configuration that's usually used for dynamic SAR in debugfs, like so:    # cat /sys/kernel/debug/iwlwifi/*/iwlmvm/tx_power_status   2.4 = 10.000 dBm   5.2L = 12.000 dBm   5.2H = 11.000 dBm  When a value hasn't been set, print &quot;(not limited)&quot; instead of &quot;value dBm&quot;.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51246 TEST=configure the TX power through power_manager or vendor_cmd, then cat the /sys/kernel/debug/iwlwifi/*/iwlmvm/tx_power_status. It shall show 3 part of TX power configured in dBm.  Change-Id: I4d1576dd95388a95d85340ada95ba34a73bc4cf2 Signed-off-by: Matt Chen &lt;matt.chen@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg &lt;johannes.berg@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Luca Coelho &lt;luciano.coelho@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394409 Commit-Ready: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="394409" owner_email="matt.chen@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/09/394409/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9929bffd0bfe643f54b5ffb2f65ddd5dfb3fb510" commit="546b9f654a91bb14a108ef2df2f000407ffc3d3b" commit_message="debugd: Replace /var/run with /run  BUG=None TEST='cat /run/arc/bugreport/pipe'  Change-Id: I9929bffd0bfe643f54b5ffb2f65ddd5dfb3fb510 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399098 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ahmed Fakhry &lt;afakhry@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399098" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/98/399098/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2b52cac57dcde12a6b7405e7d712240e278954e2" commit="79f32fff0dab31c8650e2bab89d8cb35983f58bd" commit_message="cleanup: Rename charge_temp_sensor_get_val() to charge_get_battery_temp()  charge_temp_sensor_get_val() is used to get the battery temperature value hence renamed it to charge_get_battery_temp().  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=make buildall -j  Change-Id: I2b52cac57dcde12a6b7405e7d712240e278954e2 Signed-off-by: Vijay Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/397962 Commit-Ready: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="397962" owner_email="vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/62/397962/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I5368db968c16151f32ac45a3cf8f2184afc4b281" commit="5fa094f0ac1f758e52d51bfb21283cdadfeacb15" commit_message="FROMLIST: debug: More properly delay for secondary CPUs  We've got a delay loop waiting for secondary CPUs.  That loop uses loops_per_jiffy.  However, loops_per_jiffy doesn't actually mean how many tight loops make up a jiffy on all architectures.  It is quite common to see things like this in the boot log:   Calibrating delay loop (skipped), value calculated using timer   frequency.. 48.00 BogoMIPS (lpj=24000)  In my case I was seeing lots of cases where other CPUs timed out entering the debugging only to print their stack crawls shortly after the kdb&gt; prompt was written.  It appears that other code with similar loops (like __spin_lock_debug) adds an extra __delay(1) in there which makes it work better. Presumably the __delay(1) is very safe.  At least on modern ARM/ARM64 systems it will just do a CP15 instruction, which should be safe.  On older ARM systems it will fall back to an actual delay loop, or perhaps another memory-mapped timer.  On other platforms it must be safe too or it wouldn't be used in __spin_lock_debug.  Note that we use __delay(100) instead of __delay(1) so we can get a little closer to a more accurate timeout on systems where __delay() is backed by a timer.  It's better to have a more accurate timeout and the only penalty is that we might wait an extra 99 &quot;loops&quot; before we enter the debugger.  BUG=None TEST=echo HARDLOCKUP &gt; /sys/kernel/debug/provoke-crash/DIRECT  Change-Id: I5368db968c16151f32ac45a3cf8f2184afc4b281 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9377327/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399258 Reviewed-by: Sonny Rao &lt;sonnyrao@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399258" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/58/399258/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8898.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>